# ACP daemon configuration (acp-daemon.service, systemd user unit).
#
# Installed as /etc/acp/daemon.env: the default for every user. Upgrades keep
# your edits (pacman backup file; a new default lands as daemon.env.pacnew).
# For a per-user configuration, copy this file to ~/.config/acp/daemon.env
# (chmod 600): when that file exists, its ACP_DAEMON_ARGS replaces this one.
# Apply changes with: systemctl --user restart acp-daemon
#
# The default runs the daemon with no projects and no Profile, so it starts as
# installed. Nothing here is guessed for you: projects and the Profile are
# explicit operator choices.
#
# One shell-style word list; paths must not contain spaces.
#   --allow-project NAME             allow a project (repeat per project)
#   --allow-root NAME=/abs/path      its repository root (repeat per project)
#   --database /abs/profile.sqlite3  select this existing Profile at start. Create
#                                    it first (Desktop: Profile & review, or
#                                    acp-query ... profile create <path>); the
#                                    daemon never creates or adopts one itself.
#   --agent-config /abs/file         private session configuration (optional)
#   --context-mcp /usr/bin/acp-mcp   context bridge for sessions (each start still
#                                    needs an explicit share opt-in)
#
# Example:
#   ACP_DAEMON_ARGS="--allow-project acp --allow-root acp=/home/me/code/acp --database /home/me/.local/state/acp/profile.sqlite3"
#
# Write access is never configured here: enable it per daemon run, explicitly.
ACP_DAEMON_ARGS=""
